  {{!--
    A table rather than a flex row: Gmail and Outlook drop `display:flex` and `gap` entirely,
    which left these icons flowing as inline images on a text baseline — each at whatever size
    and margin its own class happened to set, so the row came out staggered. A table row is the
    one layout primitive every mail client honours.

    All four source assets are identical 512x512 squares, so they render at one size with no
    per-icon overrides. `display:block` kills the descender gap inline images inherit from the
    line box, and `border:0` stops Outlook drawing a frame around a linked image.
  --}}
